    <!-- Info Section -->
    <section class="safari-section">
        <div class="container">
            <h2 class="section-title">Discover Chitwan's Hidden Gateway: The Amaltari Safari Experience</h2>
            <p class="safari-paragraph">
                Nestled on the western edge of Chitwan National Park lies <strong>Amaltari</strong>, a peaceful and less-traveled entry point that opens the door to some of the most remarkable wildlife and cultural experiences in Nepal. Far from the bustling tourist hubs, Amaltari offers a deeper, more intimate connection to nature, community, and adventure.
            </p>
            <p class="safari-paragraph">
                This journey takes you into the heart of <strong>Chitwan National Park</strong>, a UNESCO World Heritage Site known for its rich biodiversity and unspoiled natural beauty. Covering 932 square kilometers of dense sal forests, grasslands, and riverine habitat, the park is home to some of Asia's most iconic species—<em>one-horned rhinoceroses, Bengal tigers, Asian elephants, leopards, sloth bears</em>, and more than <strong>650 bird species</strong>.
            </p>
            <p class="safari-paragraph">
                What makes the <strong>Amaltari route</strong> unique is its community-driven approach to tourism. Here, the local <strong>Tharu community</strong> plays a central role in hosting and guiding visitors, offering authentic insights into their traditions, lifestyle, and conservation efforts.
            </p>
            <ul class="safari-list">
                <li>🛶 Glide quietly down the Narayani River on a canoe</li>
                <li>🐾 Track wild animals on a guided jungle walk</li>
                <li>🚙 Venture deep into the park on a jeep safari</li>
                <li>🌅 Witness breathtaking sunsets over the river</li>
                <li>🎶 Join cultural evenings of Tharu music and dance</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>


